#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali was told to stay behind until he had returned the deposits people had left with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "Cali waxaa loo sheegay inuu dib u haro ilaa uu ka celiyo ammaanadii dadku kaga tageen Nabiga ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Dadkii wax baadhayay ayaa aad ugu soo dhowaaday ilaa Abu Bakr uu si hoose u yidhi, “Haddii midkood hoos u eego cagihiisa, wuu na arki lahaa.” Nabigu ﷺ wuxuu ku jawaabay, “Maxaad ka malaynaysaa laba uu Alle yahay kooda saddexaad?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah recalled this moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Alle wuxuu daqiiqaddan ku xusay Quraanka: “midkii labaad ee labadii qof, markii ay ku jireen godka, markii uu ku yidhi saaxiibkiis, ‘Ha murugoon; Alle wuu inala jiraaye.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling, when the three nights had passed, Asma brought their food but had no strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and tied it on, and so she was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Werinta Ibn Ishaq, markii ay saddexdii habeen dhammaadeen, Asma waxay u keentay cuntadoodii balse may haysan suun ay ku xidhato boorsada. Waxay furtay suunkii dhexdeeda oo ay ku xidhay, sidaas darteedna waxaa loogu magac daray Gabadhii Labada Suun Lahayd."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The pursuers climbed the mountain and passed the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its opening, they said no one could have gone in there, and moved on. Ibn Kathir calls this report’s chain good."
msgstr "Dadkii eryanayay ayaa buurta koray waxayna soo mareen godka. Markii ay arkeen shabakad caaro-caaro oo ku fidsan afka godka, waxay yidhaahdeen cidina halkaas ma geli karin, wayna iska socdeen. Ibn Kathir wuxuu silsiladda werintan ku tilmaamay mid wanaagsan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some tell that the searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening, and walked on."
msgstr "Qaar waxay sheegaan in dadkii wax baadhayay ay ku arkeen shabakad caaro-caaro afka godka, dabadeedna ay iska socdeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were comes from a later biography."
msgstr "Al-Bukhari wuxuu xusayaa saddex habeen. Habeennada toddobaadka ay ahaayeen waxay ku timid taariikh-nololeed dambe."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how the two reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid there for three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay werinaysaa sida ay labadoodu u gaadheen god ku yaalla Buurta Thawr ayna halkaas ugu dhuunteen saddex habeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them and brought them news from Makkah after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay werinaysaa sida walaalkeed ‘Abdullah uu habeenada ula qaatay uguna keenay wararka Makkah marka gudcurku dhaco ka dib."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought the ewes to the cave each evening of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay werinaysaa sida ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah uu laxaha ugu keeni jiray godka fiid kasta oo ka mid ah saddexda habeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr recalls fearing that anyone who looked down at his own feet would see them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr wuxuu xasuustaa cabsidii uu ka qabay in qof kasta oo hoos u eega cagihiisa uu arki doono iyaga."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The verse speaks of the Prophet ﷺ as the second of two in the cave, telling his companion not to grieve."
msgstr "Aayaddu waxay ka hadlaysaa Nabiga ﷺ oo ahaa kii labaad ee labadii qof ee godka ku jiray, isagoo saaxiibkiis ku leh ha murugoon."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir explains the verse: Allah supported and aided His Messenger, who sheltered in the cave for three days."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir wuxuu sharxayaa aayadda: Alle wuu taageeray oo u gargaaray Rasuulkiisa, kaas oo gabbaad ka dhigtay godka muddo saddex maalmood ah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Asma tied the food bag with her waist-belt, and so was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq wuxuu werinayaa sida Asma ay boorsadii cuntada ugu xidhay suunkeeda dhexda, sidaas darteedna loogu magac daray Gabadhii Labada Suun Lahayd."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The report of the spider’s web across the cave’s opening, whose chain Ibn Kathir calls good."
msgstr "Werinta ku saabsan shabakadda caaro-caarada ee afka godka, taas oo silsiladdeeda uu Ibn Kathir ku tilmaamay mid wanaagsan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A modern biography names the three nights: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Taariikh-nololeed casri ah ayaa magacowday saddexda habeen: habeenada ka horreeyay Jimcaha, Sabtida iyo Axadda."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "The number beside each book counts its source passages."
msgstr "Lambarka ku ag yaal buug kasta waa tirada qoraallada tixraaca ee ka yimid."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid inside it. They would stay there for three nights."
msgstr "Nabiga ﷺ iyo Abu Bakr waxay gaareen god ku yaalla Buurta Thawr dhexdiisana way ku dhuunteen. Waxay halkaas joogeen saddex habeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each night, Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah slept near them. Before dawn he slipped back to Makkah, so that morning found him among Quraysh as if he had never left, and at dark he returned with any plot he had heard."
msgstr "Habeen kasta, wiilka Abu Bakr ee ‘Abdullah wuxuu seexan jiray agtooda. Waaberiga ka hor ayuu si dhuumasho ah dib ugu noqon jiray Makkah, si uu waagu ugu baryo Quraysh dhexdeeda sidii qof aan marnaba bixin, gudcurkana wuxuu ugu soo laaban jiray shirqool kasta oo uu maqlay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah grazed a few milking ewes nearby and brought them to the cave after nightfall, so the two had milk. He did this on each of the three nights."
msgstr "Abu Bakr addoonkiisii la xoreeyay ee ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wuxuu agagaarka ku daajin jiray dhowr laxaad oo caano leh, wuxuuna godka u keeni jiray markay habeenka noqoto, si ay labadoodu caano u helaan. Sidaas ayuu samayn jiray mid kasta oo saddexdii habeen ka mid ah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr slipped into a cave on Mount Thawr and stayed out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Nabiga ﷺ iyo Abuu Bakar waxay si qarsoodi ah u galeen god ku yaal Buurta Thawr, halkaas ayayna ku dhuunteen. Saddex habeen ayuu godku hoygooda qarsoon ahaa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They were not alone for long. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Muddo dheer keligood ma ay joogin. Habeen kasta, markii mugdigu dhacay, ‘Cabdullaahi, ina Abuu Bakar, ayaa u iman jiray isagoo wata wararka ku saabsan qorshayaasha Quraysh. Waaberiga ka hor ayuu si qarsoodi ah ugu noqon jiray Makkah, si subaxdii loogu arko sidii inuusan weligiis ka tegin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "And as darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought a few milking ewes to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. Every one of the three nights, he came."
msgstr "Markii mugdigu dhacay, ‘Caamir ibn Fuhayrah, oo ahaa addoonkii uu Abuu Bakar xoreeyey, ayaa dhowr laxood oo la lisay godka u keeni jiray, si labadooduba u helaan caano cusub. Saddexdii habeenba wuu iman jiray."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Markaas ayay dadkii baadi-goobayay aad ugu soo dhowaadeen, ilaa uu Abuu Bakar hoos ugu yiri, “Haddii midkood cagihiisa hoos u eego, wuu na arki lahaa.” Nabiga ﷺ ayaa ugu jawaabay, “Maxaad ka qabtaa laba uu Allah yahay kan saddexaad?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah preserved that moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah wuxuu Qur’aanka ku xafiday dhacdadaas: “markii uu ahaa kan labaad ee labada, iyagoo godka ku jira, markuu saaxiibkiis ku yiri, ‘Ha murugoon; Allah waa nala jiraa.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Late that night the Prophet ﷺ left his house and set out with Abu Bakr, who carried all his savings with him. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Habeenkaas goor dambe ayuu Nebigu ﷺ gurigiisa ka baxay, isaga oo la socda Abu Bakr oo dhammaan wixii uu kaydsaday watay. Waddada woqooyi ee Madinah uma aysan qaadin, balse koonfur ayay u leexdeen, dhanka Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night, the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr quietly left Makkah. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Habeenkaas, Nebiga ﷺ iyo Abu Bakr ayaa si aamusnaan ah uga baxay Makkah. Koonfur ayay aadeen, dhinaca ka soo horjeeda Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr. They climbed to a cave in its side and slipped inside, out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Markii ay qiyaastii shan mayl socdeen, waxay gaareen Buurta Thawr. Waxay u fuuleen god ku yaallay dhinaceeda, wayna galeen iyaga oo aan la arag. Saddex habeen ayuu godkaasi u ahaa meel ay ku dhuuntaan."

