#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The second month of the Arab calendar, in which the Prophet ﷺ left Makkah."
msgstr "Bisha labaad ee kalandarka Carabta, oo uu Nebigu ﷺ ka baxay Makkah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Muharram"
msgstr "Muxarram"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The first month of the Arab calendar."
msgstr "Bisha koowaad ee kalandarka Carabta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Dhu al-Hijjah"
msgstr "Dul-Xijjah"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The last month of the Arab calendar, the month of the pilgrimage."
msgstr "Bisha ugu dambaysa ee kalandarka Carabta, waana bisha xajka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "An open yard where dates are spread out to dry."
msgstr "Barxad furan oo timirta la fidiyo si ay u qallasho."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Bricks of clay, dried in the sun rather than fired."
msgstr "Leben dhoobo ah oo qorraxda lagu qallajiyo, halkii dab lagu adkayn lahaa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Short rhythmic verse, chanted while working or travelling."
msgstr "Tix gaaban oo miisaaman, oo la qaado marka la shaqaynayo ama la safrayo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The direction Muslims face in prayer: first Jerusalem, later the Ka‘bah."
msgstr "Jihada ay Muslimiintu u jeestaan marka ay tukanayaan: markii hore Qudus, dabadeedna Kacbada."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ka‘bah"
msgstr "Kacbada"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The cube-shaped House of Allah in Makkah, which Muslims face in prayer."
msgstr "Guriga Alle ee qaabkiisu u eg yahay cube, kuna yaal Makkah, oo Muslimiintu u jeestaan marka ay tukanayaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Measures of grain: a mudd is a double handful, and four of them make a sa‘."
msgstr "Halbeegyo lagu cabbiro badarka: mudd waa laba sacab oo buuxa, afar mudd-na waxay noqdaan hal saac."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A fragrant grass of the valleys around Makkah."
msgstr "Caws udgoon oo ka baxa dooxooyinka ku hareeraysan Makkah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Badr"
msgstr "Badar"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The first great battle between the Muslims and Quraysh, two years after the Hijrah."
msgstr "Dagaalkii weynaa ee ugu horreeyay ee dhex maray Muslimiinta iyo Quraysh, laba sano ka dib Hijrada."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Siffin"
msgstr "Siffiin"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A battle between Muslims, decades later, in the time of ‘Ali."
msgstr "Dagaal dhex maray Muslimiinta tobannaan sano ka dib, xilligii Cali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hadith"
msgstr "Xadiis"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A report of what the Prophet ﷺ said or did, passed on by named narrators."
msgstr "Warbixin ka warramaysa wixii Nebigu ﷺ yiri ama sameeyay, oo ay soo weriyeen weriyeyaal magac leh."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A report from someone who did not witness it and does not name who told him."
msgstr "Warbixin uu soo tebiyay qof aan dhacdada goobjoog u ahayn, isla markaana aan sheegin cidda uga warrantay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Salman al-Farisi"
msgstr "Salman al-Faarisi"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Persian who searched for the true religion and became a companion of the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "Nin Faaris ahaa oo raadiyey diinta runta ah, dabadeedna noqday saxaabi la socday Nabiga ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Salman"
msgstr "Salmaan"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At al-‘Aqabah one pilgrimage season, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ recited the Quran to six men from Yathrib, who lived beside Jews. “By Allah,” they said to one another, “this is the prophet the Jews threatened you with.”"
msgstr "Xilli Xajka ka mid ah, al-‘Aqabah ayuu Nebi Muxammad ﷺ lix nin oo reer Yathrib ah Qur’aanka ugu akhriyey. Waxay degganaayeen meel ay Yuhuuddu deris la ahaayeen. “Wallaahi,” ayay isku yidhaahdeen, “kani waa nebiga ay Yuhuuddu idiinku gooddidayeen.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One pilgrimage season, six men from the town of Yathrib listened to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and believed."
msgstr "Xilli Xajka ka mid ah, lix nin oo reer Yathrib ah ayaa dhegaystay Nebi Muxammad ﷺ, wayna rumaysteen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night and pledged to protect him as they protected their own women and children. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "Sannad kasta dad badan ayaa iman jiray, ilaa toddobaatan iyo saddex nin iyo laba dumar ahi ay habeenkii halkaas kula kulmeen, una ballanqaadeen inay u ilaalin doonaan sida ay u ilaaliyaan dumarkooda iyo carruurtooda. “Anigu idinkaan idinka mid ahay, idinkuna anigaa iga mid tihiin,” ayuu yidhi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came at night. They promised to keep him safe, just like their own families."
msgstr "Markii dambe, dad kale oo badan ayaa habeenkii yimid. Waxay u ballanqaadeen inay ilaalin doonaan sidii ay qoysaskooda u ilaaliyaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "“It is Yathrib,” he told his companions, and group after group they slipped away to Madinah. At last, of those free to go, only he, Abu Bakr and ‘Ali were left. And he waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "“Waa Yathrib,” ayuu asxaabtiisa u sheegay. Kooxba koox ayay si qarsoodi ah ugu ambabaxeen Madinah. Ugu dambayntii, kuwii bixi karayey waxaa hadhay isaga, Abu Bakr iyo ‘Ali oo keliya. Isaguna wuxuu sugayey oggolaanshaha Allah si uu uga daba tago."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So his friends moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "Sidaas ayay asxaabtiisu ugu guureen Yathrib, magaalada aynu Madinah u naqaan. Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu sugayey oggolaanshaha Allah si uu uga daba tago."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go. “Do not hurry,” he was told. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” So he waited, hoping it would be the Prophet ﷺ, and fed two camels for four months to have them ready."
msgstr "Abu Bakr marar badan ayuu codsaday inuu baxo. Waxaa lagu yidhi, “Ha degdegin. Waxaa laga yaabaa in Allah ku siiyo wehel.” Markaas ayuu sugay, isagoo rajaynaya in wehelkaasi noqdo Nebiga ﷺ. Afar bilood ayuu laba awr quudinayey si ay ugu diyaar ahaadaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr wanted to go too. He was told to wait: perhaps Allah would give him a companion."
msgstr "Abu Bakr isaguna wuxuu doonayey inuu baxo. Waxaa lagu yidhi ha sugo; waxaa laga yaabaa in Allah wehel siiyo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one day, in the full heat of noon, the Prophet ﷺ came at an hour he never came, and said, “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “Companionship?” Abu Bakr asked. “Companionship.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Maalin maalmaha ka mid ah, kulaylkii duhurka ugu darnaa, ayuu Nebigu ﷺ yimid xilli aanu caadi ahaan iman jirin, wuxuuna yidhi, “Allah wuxuu ii oggolaaday inaan baxo.” Abu Bakr ayaa weydiiyey, “Wehel?” “Wehel,” ayuu ku jawaabay. Abu Bakr farxad ayuu la ooyey."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon, the Prophet ﷺ came with the news: they could go together! Abu Bakr cried for joy."
msgstr "Duhur kulul ayuu Nebigu ﷺ la yimid warka: way wada safri karaan! Abu Bakr farxad ayuu la ooyey."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels to the cave of Thawr after three nights. Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Waxay kireysteen hage u keena awrta godka Thawr saddex habeen ka dib. Asma, oo ahayd gabadha Abu Bakr, ma haysan wax ay cuntada ku xidho, markaasay suunkeedii dhexda laba u kala jeexday. Sidaas ayay ku noqotay “tii labada suun lahayd”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two and used that."
msgstr "Asma ma haysan wax ay cuntada ku xidho, markaasay suunkeedii dhexda laba u kala jeexday oo ku xidhatay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, Quraysh had watched his companions go, and feared he would follow. In Dar al-Nadwah their leaders took Abu Jahl’s plan: young men from every clan would strike him together, spreading his blood across them all."
msgstr "Makkah gudaheeda, Quraysh waxay arkeen asxaabtiisa oo baxaya, waxayna ka baqeen inuu isaguna daba tago. Dar al-Nadwah, hoggaamiyayaashoodu waxay qaateen qorshihii Abu Jahl: dhallinyaro qabiil kasta ka socota ayaa si wadajir ah u dili lahayd, si dhiiggiisu qabiilooyinka oo dhan ugu qaybsamo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The leaders of Makkah were afraid of the Prophet ﷺ, and they made a plan to attack him."
msgstr "Hoggaamiyayaashii Makkah waxay ka baqeen Nebiga ﷺ, waxayna qorsheeyeen inay weeraraan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night the men gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak. “Sleep in it,” he said. “Nothing you dislike will reach you from them.”"
msgstr "Habeenkaas nimankii waxay isugu yimaadeen albaabkiisa, iyagoo sugaya inuu seexdo. Wuxuu ‘Ali ku yidhi sariirtiisa ha ku seexdo, isagoo ku duuban khamiiskiisa cagaaran. “Ku seexo,” ayuu yidhi. “Wax aad neceb tahay oo dhankooda ka imanaya kuma gaadhi doono.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "Habeenkaas waxay ku sugeen bannaanka albaabkiisa. ‘Ali wuxuu jiifay sariirta Nebiga, isagoo ku duuban khamiiskiisa cagaaran."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting, “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Dabadeed wuxuu ula baxay cantoobo ciid ah, madaxyadoodana ku firdhiyey isagoo akhrinaya, “Sidaas ayaannu u daboolnay, mana arkayaan.” Allah ayaa ka qariyey araggooda, wuuna sii socday."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, scattering dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Nebigu ﷺ hortooda ayuu si toos ah uga gudbay isagoo ciid firdhinaya, Allahna wuu ka qariyey inay arkaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of the house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Wuxuu u yimid Abu Bakr, labadooduna waxay ka baxeen albaab yar oo guriga gadaashiisa ku yaallay, Abu Bakrna wuxuu sitay dhammaan wixii uu kaydsaday. Waddada woqooyi ee Madinah uma ay dhaqaaqin; koonfur ayay u jeesteen, dhanka Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Isaga iyo saaxiibkiisii ugu dhowaa, Abu Bakr, ayaa mugdiga si qarsoodi ah ku baxay. Koonfur ayay aadeen, dhankii ka soo horjeeday Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr and a cave in its side. Abu Bakr went in first, feeling his way in the dark, ready to take any harm himself. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Markay qiyaastii shan mayl socdeen, waxay gaadheen Buurta Thawr iyo god dhinaceeda ku yaal. Abu Bakr ayaa marka hore galay, isagoo mugdiga isku taataabanaya, diyaarna u ah inuu isagu dhib kasta qaato. Saddex habeen ayuu godku u noqon lahaa meel ay ku dhuuntaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They reached a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Waxay gaadheen god ku yaal Buurta Thawr. Abu Bakr ayaa marka hore galay si uu u hubiyo inuu ammaan yahay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove the flock along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out his footprints."
msgstr "Markii mugdigu dhacay, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, oo ahaa addoonkii la xoreeyey ee Abu Bakr, ayaa idihiisii caanaha laga lisay godka keenay, si labadoodu caano cusub u helaan. Waaberigii ayuu adhiga ku mariyey raadkii ‘Abdullah, idihiina raadkiisii bay tirtireen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Amir brought sheep every evening for milk. In the morning, the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir fiid kasta wuxuu ido u keeni jiray si ay caano uga helaan. Subaxdii, iduhu waxay dul mari jireen raadkii ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Searchers stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid they would look down. The Prophet ﷺ calmed his friend."
msgstr "Baadigoobayaashu waxay istaageen godka korkiisa! Abu Bakr wuxuu ka baqay inay hoos u soo eegaan. Nebigu ﷺ saaxiibkiis ayuu dejiyey."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the guide came with the camels, as arranged, and now there were four of them, with ‘Amir riding behind Abu Bakr. The guide led them down below Makkah and out along the coast, “by the edge of the sea.”"
msgstr "Markaasaa hagihii la yimid geeli, sidii la isku ogaa. Hadda waxay ahaayeen afar neef, ‘Amirna wuxuu ka raacay Abu Bakr gadaashiisa. Haguhu wuxuu ka kaxeeyey meel ka hooseysa Makkah, wuxuuna ku hoggaamiyey xeebta, “cirifka badda agteeda.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights, their guide came with the camels, and they rode out along the coast by the sea."
msgstr "Saddex habeen ka dib, hagahoodii ayaa geeli ula yimid, dabadeedna waxay raaceen xeebta badda agteeda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People on the road knew Abu Bakr, but not the man with him. “Who is this man in front of you?” they asked. “This man guides me on the way,” he answered. They thought he meant the road; he meant the way of good."
msgstr "Dadkii jidka joogay way garanayeen Abu Bakr, laakiin ma ay garanayn ninka la socday. “Waa kuma ninkan kaa horreeya?” ayay weydiiyeen. “Waa ninkan jidka igu haga,” ayuu ku jawaabay. Waxay u qaateen inuu jidka caadiga ah ka hadlayo; isaguse wuxuu ula jeeday jidka khayrka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People asked Abu Bakr who was with him. “He guides me on the way,” he said: the way of good."
msgstr "Dadku waxay Abu Bakr weydiiyeen ninka la socda. “Wuxuu igu haga jidka,” ayuu yidhi, isagoo ula jeeda jidka khayrka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh had put a price on the two. A man told Suraqah ibn Malik he had seen dark figures by the coast. “I knew that it was them,” Suraqah said, but he told the man otherwise. He wanted the hundred camels for himself."
msgstr "Quraysh waxay abaalmarin u ballanqaadeen cidda keenta labadooda. Nin ayaa Suraqah ibn Malik u sheegay inuu xeebta ku arkay dad mugdi u eg. “Waan gartay inay iyagu ahaayeen,” ayuu Suraqah yidhi, balse ninkii wax kale ayuu u sheegay. Isagu wuxuu doonayay inuu boqolka geel ah keligiis helo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road by the sea, a rider called Suraqah raced after them on his horse, hoping for a big reward."
msgstr "Jidka badda agteeda, nin la odhan jiray Suraqah ayaa faraskiisa kula orday, isagoo rajaynaya abaalmarin weyn."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then his horse’s forelegs sank into the ground up to the knees, and Suraqah fell."
msgstr "Si xawli ah ayuu u watay faraskiisa ilaa uu maqlay Nebiga ﷺ oo akhrinaya. Nebigu ﷺ dib uma soo eegin; Abu Bakrse marar badan ayuu gadaal u eegay. Markaas ayay lugihii hore ee farasku dhulka ugu godmeen ilaa jilbaha, Suraqahna wuu dhacay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah called out for safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Suraqah ayaa ammaan dalbaday, wuxuuna u bandhigay sahay. Wax keliya ayay ka codsadeen: “Meesha aan joogno qari.” ‘Amir ayaa maqaar ugu qoray warqad ammaan ah, Suraqahna dib ayuu u noqday, isagoo eryadayaashii kale mid mid dib ugu celiyey."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him only to keep their secret, and he sent the other riders home."
msgstr "Suraqah wuu ka tanaasulay daba-galkii. Waxay ka codsadeen oo keliya inuu sirtooda qariyo, wuxuuna fardooleyda kale dib ugu celiyey guryahooda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They rode on, but their food had run out in a year of drought. By the road stood the two tents of Umm Ma‘bad, a woman who gave water and food to those who passed. They asked to buy meat and dates, but she had none."
msgstr "Way sii socdeen, laakiin cuntadoodii way ka dhammaatay xilli abaar ah. Jidka dhinaciisa waxaa yiilay labada teendho ee Umm Ma‘bad, oo ahayd haweeney biyo iyo cunto siin jirtay dadka jidka maraya. Waxay ka codsadeen inay ka iibsadaan hilib iyo timir, balse waxba ma ay haysan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Iyagoo gaajaysan oo gurigooda ka fog ayay istaageen teendhada Umm Ma‘bad. Wax cunto ah oo ay siiso ma ay haysan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the back of her tent stood a ewe too weak to follow the flock. The Prophet ﷺ passed his hand over her udder, spoke the name of Allah, and milked until froth rose over the vessel. Umm Ma‘bad drank first, he drank last."
msgstr "Teendhada gadaasheeda waxaa taagnayd lax tabar daran oo aan adhiga raaci karin. Nebigu ﷺ gacantiisa ayuu ku masaxay candhada, magaca Allah ayuu ku dhawaaqay, dabadeedna wuu lisay ilaa xumbadu ka buuxsantay weelkii. Umm Ma‘bad ayaa ugu horrayn cabtay, isagaana ugu dambayn cabbay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked her, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Laxdeeda caatada ahi caano ma lahayn. Nebigu ﷺ magaca Allah ayuu ku dhawaaqay oo wuu lisay, dabadeedna qof kastaa wuu cabbay!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she described their guest: a man of shining beauty, his words like beads slipping from a string. “By Allah,” said Abu Ma‘bad, “that is the man from Quraysh.”"
msgstr "Markii ninkeedii guriga yimid, waxay uga warrantay martidoodii: nin quruxdiisu iftiimaysay, hadalkiisuna u ekaa kuul xarig ka sii siibanaya. “Allah baan ku dhaartaye,” ayuu yidhi Abu Ma‘bad, “waa ninkii Quraysh.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she told him about their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Markii ninkeedii guriga yimid, waxay uga warrantay martidoodii: weji ifaya iyo hadal u eg kuul xarig ku taxan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Muslims of Madinah watched for him till the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is your good fortune, the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Subax kasta muslimiinta Madinah way sugi jireen ilaa kulaylku ku khasbo inay gudaha galaan. Markaas ayaa nin qalcad ku jiray arkay socdaalayaal dhar cad qaba oo hawada kulul ka dhex muuqda: “Waa kan nasiibkiinnii wanaagsan, kii aad sugayseen!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people waited every morning in the hot sun. At last a man shouted: he is here!"
msgstr "Madinah, dadku subax kasta waxay ku sugi jireen qorraxda kulul. Ugu dambayn nin ayaa qayliyey: “Waa yimid!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, in the shade of a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and they greeted Abu Bakr. Then the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr held his cloak over him, and at that they knew him."
msgstr "Waxay Quba ka heleen isagoo timir hoosteeda, Abu Bakrna la joogo. Intooda badan hore uma ay arag, sidaas darteed waxay salaameen Abu Bakr. Markaas ayay qorraxdu ku dhacday Nebiga ﷺ, Abu Bakrna go’iisii ayuu ku hadheeyey; markaas ayay garteen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him resting in the shade of a palm tree at Quba, with Abu Bakr beside him."
msgstr "Waxay Quba ka heleen isagoo ku nasanaya hooska geed timireed, Abu Bakrna dhinaciisa joogo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There ‘Ali caught up with him, after three days in Makkah returning what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. The Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque at Quba and prayed in it, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "Halkaas ayuu ‘Ali kula kulmay, ka dib markii uu saddex maalmood Makkah ku sugnaa si uu dadkii ugu celiyo wixii ay u dhiibteen Nebiga ﷺ. Nebigu ﷺ Quba ayuu ka dhisay masaajidkiisii, wuuna ku tukaday. Jimce ayuu haddana u fuulay jidka Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba he built a mosque and prayed in it. Then he rode on into Madinah."
msgstr "Quba ayuu masaajid ka dhisay oo ku tukaday. Dabadeedna wuxuu u sii kicitimay Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way he prayed his first Friday prayer in Madinah. Clan after clan came out: “Stay with us. We have the numbers and the strength.” Each time he said of his camel, “Let her go her way; she is under orders.”"
msgstr "Jidka ayuu ku tukaday salaaddii Jimcaha ee ugu horreysay ee Madinah. Reerba reerka ka dambeeya ayaa u soo baxay: “Nala joog. Tiro iyo awoodba waan haysannaa.” Mar kasta wuxuu geeliisa ka odhan jiray: “U daaya inay jidkeeda marto; amar baa la siiyey.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah. Family after family asked him to stay, but he let his camel walk on."
msgstr "Ugu dambayn Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu fuulay oo galay Madinah. Qoysba qoyska ka dambeeya ayaa ka codsaday inuu la joogo, balse wuxuu daayey geeliisii inay sii socoto."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The whole town poured out, and women on the rooftops strained to see: “Which one is he?” At last the camel knelt in a yard where dates were laid to dry. “This, if Allah wills, is the stopping place,” he said."
msgstr "Magaalada oo dhan ayaa bannaanka u soo baxday, dumarkii saqafyada saarnaana waxay isku dayayeen inay arkaan: “Kee buu yahay?” Ugu dambayn hashii waxay jilba joogsatay barxad timirta lagu qalajinayey. “Halkan, haddii Allah idmo, ayaynu degaynaa,” ayuu yidhi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Children ran and people climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried."
msgstr "Carruur ayaa orodday, dadkuna meelaha dhaadheer ayay fuuleen si ay u arkaan. Hashiisu waxay jilba joogsatay barxad timirta lagu qalajinayey."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There his mosque rose, from bricks of sun-dried clay. The Prophet ﷺ carried them with the others, chanting, “O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so help the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
msgstr "Halkaas ayay masaajidkiisu ka taagnaatay, oo laga dhisay leben dhoobo ah oo qorraxda lagu qalajiyey. Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu la qaaday lebenka dadkii kale, isagoo ku celcelinaya: “Allow, khayr ma jiro aan ahayn khayrka Aakhiro, ee u gargaar Ansaar iyo Muhaajiriinta.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There they built a mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ carried bricks to help."
msgstr "Halkaas ayay masaajid ka dhiseen, Nebiguna ﷺ wuxuu caawiyey isagoo leben qaaday."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the fever of Madinah laid his companions low. Makkah had been the dearest of lands to him, and now he prayed for their new home: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Dabadeed qandhada Madinah ayaa saaxiibbadiis ku ridday xanuun. Makkah waxay ahayd dhulka ugu qaalisan qalbigiisa, haddana wuxuu u duceeyey hoygooda cusub: “Allow, Madinah nooga dhig mid aan u jecelnahay sida aad Makkah nooga dhigtay, ama ka sii jeclaan badan.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make Madinah as dear to them as Makkah, and even dearer."
msgstr "Wuxuu Alle ka baryey inuu Madinah uga dhigo mid ay u jecel yihiin sida Makkah, kana sii jeclaan badan."

