#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Kuwa baadi-goobayaashu aad bay ugu soo dhowaadeen, ilaa Abu Bakr uu hoos u yiri: “Haddii midkood cagihiisa hoos u eego, wuu ina arki lahaa.” Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu ku jawaabay: “Maxaad ka qabtaa laba uu Allah yahay ka saddexaad?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Nor were they alone. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Keligoodna ma ahayn. Habeen kasta, wiilka Abu Bakr ee ‘Abdullah ayaa mugdiga ka dib u iman jiray, isagoo wata wararka ku saabsan qorshayaasha Quraysh, dabadeedna waaberiga ka hor ayuu si dhuumasho ah ugu noqon jiray Makkah, si subaxdii loogu arko halkaas sidii inuusan waligiis ka tegin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A home had to be offered before anyone could leave: the pledges at al-‘Aqabah gave the believers somewhere to go."
msgstr "Ka hor intaan qofna bixi karin, waa in meel hoy loo helo: ballamihii al-‘Aqabah waxay mu’miniinta siiyeen meel ay aadaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Waiting on Allah’s permission and preparing every detail went together: camels fed for months, a guide hired, food packed."
msgstr "Sugidda oggolaanshaha Allah iyo diyaarinta faahfaahin kasta way isla socdeen: geelu bilo ayuu quudinayay, hage ayaa la kiraystay, cuntadana waa la sii diyaariyay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His honesty held even then: on the night Quraysh plotted his death, he left ‘Ali to return all that Makkah had entrusted to him."
msgstr "Daacadnimadiisu weli way taagnayd: habeenkii ay Quraysh ku shirqoolaysay dilkiisa, wuxuu ‘Ali uga tagay inuu u celiyo wixii ay reer Makkah u dhiibteen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the most frightening moment came the calmest words: “Do not grieve; Allah is with us.”"
msgstr "Xilligii ugu cabsida badnaa ayay yimaadeen erayadii ugu degganaa: “Ha murugoon; Allah waa nala jiraa.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hunted as they were, they kept to the truth: “This man guides me on the way,” Abu Bakr said, and meant the way of good."
msgstr "Iyagoo la baadi-goobayo, haddana runta ayay ku adkaysteen: “Ninkani jidka ayuu igu hagayaa,” ayuu Abu Bakr yidhi, isagoo ula jeeday jidka khayrka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hearts can turn in a moment: the man who rode out to capture them rode back to send every pursuer home."
msgstr "Quluubtu ilbidhiqsi ayay isu beddeli kartaa: ninkii u baxay inuu qabto ayuu dib ugu noqday si uu eryade kasta ugu celiyo gurigiisa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Blessing came to a tent with nothing to give, and the Prophet ﷺ, who brought it, drank last of all."
msgstr "Barako ayaa timid teendho aan waxba bixin karin, Nebiga ﷺ ee barakada keenayna ugu dambayn ayuu cabbay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded the first mosque where he prayed openly with his companions, a mosque built on God-consciousness."
msgstr "Quba ayuu Nebiga ﷺ ka aasaasay masaajidkii ugu horreeyay ee uu si furan ula tukaday asxaabtiisa; masaajid lagu dhisay Alle-ka-cabsi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah became home by being built together: emigrants and Ansar raised the mosque side by side, and were made brothers."
msgstr "Madinah waxay hoy ku noqotay dhisme wadajir ah: muhaajiriinta iyo Ansaaru garab-iyo-garab ayay masaajidka u dhiseen, walaalona waa la isu ka dhigay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "You followed the Hijrah from a promise made by night at al-‘Aqabah to a prayer for Madinah: a long wait, three nights in a cave, a hunter turned protector, and a whole town out to welcome him."
msgstr "Waxaad raacday Hijrada laga soo bilaabo ballan habeenkii lagu galay al-‘Aqabah ilaa salaad Madinah lagu tukaday: sugitaan dheer, saddex habeen oo god lagu jiray, ugaarsade isu beddelay ilaaliye, iyo magaalo dhan oo u soo baxday inay soo dhawaysato."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His home, where he waited for permission and from where he slipped out by night with Abu Bakr."
msgstr "Gurigiisii, halkaas oo uu oggolaanshaha ku sugayay, habeenkiina uu Abu Bakr kala baxay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr hid in a cave for three nights while Quraysh searched for them."
msgstr "Meeshii Nebiga ﷺ iyo Abu Bakr saddex habeen god ku dhuunteen iyadoo Quraysh baadi-goobaysay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down to the sea and along the shore, station after station, towards Madinah."
msgstr "Haguhu wuxuu badda u soo dejiyay, wuxuuna xeebta ku hoggaamiyay, meelba meel, iyagoo u socda Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where Madinah’s Muslims first met him, under a palm, and where he founded his mosque."
msgstr "Meeshii Muslimiinta Madinah markii ugu horraysay kula kulmeen, geed timireed hoostiis, halkaas oo uu masaajidkiisa ka aasaasay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where his camel knelt, his mosque rose, and the emigrants made a new home."
msgstr "Meeshii awrkiisu fariistay, masaajidkiisu ka dhismay, muhaajiriintuna hoy cusub ka samaysteen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Under Abu Ayyub’s roof"
msgstr "Guriga Abu Ayyub hoostiisa"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Ayyub carried the Prophet’s ﷺ saddle into his house. One day a jar of water broke upstairs, and he and his wife soaked it up with their only blanket, so that not a drop would fall on their guest."
msgstr "Abu Ayyub wuxuu gurigiisa soo geliyay kooraddii Nebiga ﷺ. Maalin, weel biyo ah ayaa dabaqa sare ku jabay, isaga iyo xaaskiisuna waxay biyihii ku qallajiyeen bustahooda keliya si aan dhibicna ugu soo daadan martidooda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When water spilled upstairs, Abu Ayyub and his wife mopped it up with their only blanket, so none dripped on him."
msgstr "Markii biyo dabaqa sare ku daateen, Abu Ayyub iyo xaaskiisu waxay ku qallajiyeen bustahooda keliya si aan waxba ugu soo daadan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "She of the two waistbands"
msgstr "Gabadha labada dhex-xidh leh"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In another telling, it was at the cave that Asma’s waistband served them. She had brought their food but forgotten a strap to hang it by, so she split her waistband in two and hung the bag with one half."
msgstr "Sida sheeko kale lagu sheegay, godka ayay dhex-xidhka Asma u adeegay. Waxay u keentay cuntadoodii, balse waxay illowday xarig ay ku sudho; markaas ayay dhex-xidhkeedii laba u kala jeexday, bacdana badhkiis ayay ku xidhay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food bag, so she split her waistband in two and used one half."
msgstr "Asma ma haysan wax ay bacda cuntada ku xidho, markaas ayay dhex-xidhkeedii laba u kala jeexday oo badhkiis adeegsatay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ made each emigrant a brother to one of the Ansar who had taken them in. Each pair stood by the other and shared what they had, and at first such brothers even inherited from one another."
msgstr "Nebigu ﷺ muhaajir kasta wuxuu walaal uga dhigay mid ka mid ah Ansaar oo hoy siiyay. Lammaane kastaa midba midka kale ayuu garab istaagay, wixii ay haysteenna way wadaageen; bilowgiina walaalahaas xitaa way is dhaxli jireen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He made each newcomer a brother to someone from Madinah, so they would help each other and share."
msgstr "Qof kasta oo yimid wuxuu walaal uga dhigay qof Madinah deggan, si ay isu caawiyaan oo wax u wadaagaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Let her go her way"
msgstr "U daa jidkeeda"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Even his mother’s kin, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, called out, “Come to your mother’s people.” “Let her go her way,” he said. “She is under orders.” She walked on, and knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Xitaa qaraabadiisii dhinaca hooyada, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, ayaa ku dhawaaqay, “U kaalay dadkii hooyadaa.” Wuxuu yidhi, “U daa jidkeeda. Amar ayay ku socotaa.” Way sii socotay, waxayna ku fariisatay Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar dhexdooda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Everyone wanted the Prophet ﷺ to stay with them. “Let my camel go,” he said. “She knows where to stop.”"
msgstr "Qof kastaa wuxuu doonayay in Nebiga ﷺ uu la joogo. “Geela iska daa,” ayuu yiri. “Way garanaysaa halka ay joogsanayso.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode out of Quba on a Friday. On the way, the time for prayer came among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, and he prayed it in their mosque in the valley of Ranuna: his first Friday prayer in Madinah."
msgstr "Maalin Jimce ah ayuu Quba ka baxay isagoo geeli saaran. Intii uu jidka ku jiray, waqtigii salaaddu wuxuu ku soo beegmay Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, wuxuuna salaadda ku tukaday masaajidkooda ku yaal dooxada Ranuna. Waxay ahayd salaaddiisii Jimcaha ee ugu horraysay ee Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On his way into Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ stopped to lead the Friday prayer for the very first time there."
msgstr "Intii uu Madinah ku sii socday, Nebiga ﷺ ayaa istaagay si uu halkaas ugu tukiyo salaaddii Jimcaha ee ugu horraysay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Dressed in white"
msgstr "Dharkii caddaanka ahaa"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road they met al-Zubayr, coming home from Syria with Muslim merchants, and he dressed the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr in white. It was in white, shimmering in the mirage, that they were first seen from Madinah."
msgstr "Jidka ayay kula kulmeen al-Zubayr, oo Suuriya ka soo laabanayay isagoo la socda ganacsato Muslimiin ah. Wuxuu Nebiga ﷺ iyo Abu Bakr siiyay dhar cad. Iyagoo dharkaas cad xiran oo hilaaca saxaraha ka dhex muuqda ayaa markii ugu horraysay laga arkay Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way, their friend al-Zubayr gave them white clothes to wear."
msgstr "Jidka ayay kula kulmeen saaxiibkood al-Zubayr, wuxuuna siiyay dhar cad oo ay xidhaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As he came, the women and children of Madinah sang: “The full moon has risen over us, from the passes of al-Wada‘. Thanks are due from us, as long as anyone calls to Allah.”"
msgstr "Markii uu yimid, haweenka iyo carruurta Madinah ayaa ku heesay: “Dayaxii buuxsamay ayaa korkayaga ka soo baxay, dhinaca buuraha al-Wada‘. Mahadna waa nagu waajib, inta uu jiro qof Allah u yeedhaya.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The women and children sang a song of welcome: “The full moon has risen over us!”"
msgstr "Haweenka iyo carruurtu waxay ku qaabileen hees: “Dayaxii buuxsamay ayaa korkayaga ka soo baxay!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "South, not north"
msgstr "Koonfur, ee ma aha waqooyi"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah lay to the north, but that was not the road they took. Under cover of night they turned the opposite way, south on the road towards Yemen, and went about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah waxay ka xigtay waqooyi, laakiin jidkaas ma ay qaadin. Habeenkii ayay dhinaca kale u leexdeen, koonfurta dhanka Yemen, waxayna ilaa shan mayl u socdeen Buurta Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah was to the north, but they went south first, to a mountain called Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah waxay ka xigtay waqooyi, laakiin marka hore koonfur ayay aadeen, buur la yidhaahdo Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The road by the sea"
msgstr "Jidka badda mara"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down below Makkah and along the coast, out onto the road below ‘Usfan. Then he took them by lower Amaj, and back to the road past Qudayd, one station after another."
msgstr "Haguhu wuxuu ka dejiyay dhinaca koonfureed ee Makkah, wuxuuna ku wehelshay xeebta ilaa jidka ka hooseeya ‘Usfan. Dabadeed wuxuu mariyay Amajta hoose, kuna soo celiyay jidka ag mara Qudayd, meelba meel ka dambaysa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their guide knew the desert well. He led them down to the sea and along the coast, from one place to the next."
msgstr "Hagahoodu si fiican ayuu u yaqaannay saxaraha. Wuxuu u kaxeeyay dhanka badda, xeebtana ku sii watay, meelba meel."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In the full heat of noon, someone called to Abu Bakr: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the door, his head covered, at an hour he never came. “Allah has given me permission to leave,” he said."
msgstr "Duhurkii oo kulaylku aad u daran yahay, ayaa qof Abu Bakr ugu yeedhay: Rasuulka Allah ﷺ ayaa albaabka taagan, madaxa oo daboolan, saacad aanu caadi ahaan iman jirin. “Allah ayaa ii oggolaaday inaan baxo,” ayuu yiri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon the Prophet ﷺ knocked at Abu Bakr’s door with big news: “Allah has given me permission to leave.”"
msgstr "Maalin duhurkeed oo kulul, Nebiga ﷺ ayaa albaabka Abu Bakr soo garaacay isagoo wata war weyn: “Allah ayaa ii oggolaaday inaan baxo.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "All his money"
msgstr "Lacagtiisii oo dhan"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When Abu Bakr slipped out with the Prophet ﷺ that night, by a small door at the back of his house, he carried all his money with him: five or six thousand dirhams."
msgstr "Habeenkaas, markii Abu Bakr iyo Nebigu ﷺ ay ka baxeen albaab yar oo gurigiisa gadaashiisa ku yaallay, wuxuu watay lacagtiisii oo dhan: shan ama lix kun oo dirham."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him for the journey, thousands of silver coins."
msgstr "Abu Bakr wuxuu safarka u qaatay lacagtiisii oo dhan, kumannaan qadaadiic oo lacag ah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the mountain the trail grew confused, so the searchers climbed it and passed by the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its entrance, they said, “If anyone had gone in here, there would be no web over it.”"
msgstr "Markii raadku buurta ku dhex lumay, kuwii baadhayay ayaa fuulay oo godka ag maray. Markay arkeen xuub caaro oo afka godka qariyay, waxay yidhaahdeen: “Haddii qof halkan galay, xuubkani ma dul yaalleen.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening. “No one went in there,” they said, and walked on."
msgstr "Kuwii baadhayay waxay arkeen xuub caaro oo afka godka qariyay. “Qofna gudaha ma gelin,” ayay yidhaahdeen, wayna sii socdeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were was worked out by later biographers."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay sheegtay in la joogay saddex habeen. Taariikhyahanno dambe ayaa go’aamiyay habeenada toddobaadka ay ahaayeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Into Madinah, on a Friday"
msgstr "Madinah oo la galay maalin Jimce ah"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Jimce, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 Sebtembar 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq gives the Friday he left Quba; the day of the month was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq wuxuu sheegay Jimcihii uu Quba ka baxay; maalinta bisha waxaa go’aamiyay taariikhyahan casri ah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide comes with the camels"
msgstr "Haguhu wuxuu la yimaadaa geela"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Night of 1 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 September 622"
msgstr "Habeenka 1-da Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 Sebtembar 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came after the third night, as agreed. Later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Wuxuu yimid habeenkii saddexaad, sidii lagu heshiiyey. Taariikhyahannadii dambe waxay ku qoreen inuu yimid habeenka Isniinta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He had stayed on in Makkah through Muharram and Safar. The exact night was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Wuxuu Makkah sii joogay intii lagu jiray Muxarram iyo Safar. Habeenka saxda ah waxaa xisaabiyey taariikhyahan casri ah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Monday in Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"
msgstr "Maalin Isniin ah oo ka mid ah Rabi‘ al-Awwal · Sebtembar 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree it was a Monday. Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth of the month; others give other days."
msgstr "Warbixinnadu waxay isku raacsan yihiin inay ahayd maalin Isniin ah. Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu sheegay maalintii laba iyo tobnaad ee bisha; kuwo kalena waxay sheegeen maalmo kale."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah on their trail"
msgstr "Suraaqah oo raadkooda ku jira"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Tuesday, after the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Maalin Talaado ah, ka dib nasashadii duhur ee Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d gives this day; the other reports tell what happened in order, but name no day."
msgstr "Ibn Sacad wuxuu xusay maalintan; warbixinnada kale waxay dhacdooyinka u sheegaan siday u kala horreeyeen, balse ma xusaan maalin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "From four days to fourteen nights"
msgstr "Afar maalmood ilaa afar iyo toban habeen"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq counts Monday to Thursday; ‘Urwah speaks of ten nights and more, and Anas of fourteen."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu tirinayaa Isniinta ilaa Khamiista; Curwah wuxuu sheegayaa toban habeen iyo ka badan, Anasna afar iyo toban."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how many went ahead to Madinah, while Abu Bakr held himself back to travel with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay sheegaysaa intii ka horraysay u ambabaxday Madinah, halka Abu Bakr uu dib u dhigtay safarkiisa si uu ula safro Nebiga ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah recalls the family making them ready in haste, and Asma tying the food bag with a piece of her waistband."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay xusuusataa in qoysku degdeg ugu diyaariyey, Asma-na ay kiishkii cuntada ku xidhay qayb ka mid ah suunkeeda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them, was among Quraysh by morning, and brought their news after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay sheegaysaa sida walaalkeed ‘Abdullah habeenada ula joogay, subaxdii uga dhex muuqday Quraysh, dabadeedna mugdiga ka dib ugu keenay wararkooda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave after nightfall, on each of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay sheegaysaa sida ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah habeen kasta oo saddexda habeen ah, mugdiga ka dib, idihiisa la lisayo ugu keenay godka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how they hired a skilled guide of Banu al-Dil, gave him their two camels, and set the meeting at Thawr."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay sheegaysaa sida ay u kireysteen hage xirfad leh oo ka tirsanaa Banu al-Dil, ugu dhiibeen labadooda geel, kulankana ugu ballameen Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah and the guide set out with them, and how the guide took them by the coast road."
msgstr "‘Aishah waxay sheegaysaa sida ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah iyo haguhu ula ambabaxeen, iyo sida haguhu ugu maray jidka xeebta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how Madinah heard he had left Makkah, and how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf for ten nights and more."
msgstr "‘Urwah wuxuu sheegayaa sida Madinah looga maqlay inuu Makkah ka baxay, iyo sida uu toban habeen iyo ka badan ula joogay Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how the yard was built into a mosque, with the Prophet ﷺ carrying bricks alongside the builders."
msgstr "‘Urwah wuxuu sheegayaa sida barxaddii loogu dhisay masaajid, Nebiga ﷺ-na uu lebenka ula qaadayay dhisayaasha."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls the blood-money offered for each of the two, and a man who had just seen dark figures by the coast."
msgstr "Suraaqah wuxuu xusuustaa diyadii loo ballanqaaday qof kasta oo labadaas ah, iyo nin hadda uun xeebta agteeda ku arkay dad madow oo muuqaal ah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah describes hearing the Prophet ﷺ recite, Abu Bakr looking back, and his own horse sinking to its knees."
msgstr "Suraaqah wuxuu ka warramayaa inuu maqlay Nebiga ﷺ oo akhrinaya, Abu Bakr oo dib u eegaya, iyo faraskiisa oo jilbaha dhulka la galay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls that they took nothing he offered and asked only for secrecy, and that ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather."
msgstr "Suraaqah wuxuu xusuustaa inaysan qaadan wax uu u bandhigay, balse ay ka codsadeen oo keliya inuu arrinta qariyo; ‘Amirna uu maqaar ugu qoray warqad ammaan ah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, founded the mosque built on God-consciousness, and prayed in it."
msgstr "‘Urwah wuxuu sheegayaa sida uu ula joogay Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, u aasaasay masaajidka lagu dhisay Alle ka cabsiga, uguna tukaday."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how people walked beside his camel until she knelt where his mosque now stands, then a yard for drying dates."
msgstr "‘Urwah wuxuu sheegayaa sida dadku ula socdeen geela ilaa ay fariisatay meeshii masaajidkiisu hadda ka taagan yahay, oo markaas ahayd barxad timirta lagu qallajiyo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Quraysh, now afraid of him, met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled all their affairs."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu sheegayaa sida Quraysh, oo hadda isaga ka baqaysay, ugu kulmeen Daar al-Nadwah, gurigii ay dhammaan arrimahooda ku go’aansan jireen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Seeing the men at his door, the Prophet ﷺ tells ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak, and promises him safety."
msgstr "Markuu arkay nimankii albaabkiisa taagan, Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu Cali ku yidhi inuu sariirtiisa ku seexdo, bustihiisa cagaaranna isku duubo, wuxuuna u ballanqaaday inuu nabadgeli doono."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells why ‘Ali stayed behind: anyone in Makkah who feared for something precious had left it with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu sheegay sababta Cali uga hadhay: qof kasta oo Makkah jooga oo ka baqayay in wax qaali ahi ka lumaan, wuxuu u dhiibtay Nebiga ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling she has no food and only dry ewes; he milks one until the bowl froths: “Drink, Umm Ma‘bad.”"
msgstr "Sida uu Ibn Isxaaq sheegay, wax cunto ah ma haysan, idaha ay haysatayna caano ma lahayn. Wuxuu mid ka mid ah lisay ilaa caanuhu maddiibadda ka xumbeeyeen: “Cab, Umm Ma‘bad.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah remembers the noon visit, and Abu Bakr asking at once to go with him: “Companionship?” “Yes.”"
msgstr "Caa’isha waxay xusuusataa booqashadii duhurka iyo Abuu Bakr oo markiiba weydiistay inuu la socdo: “Ma kula saaxiib noqdaa?” “Haa.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma recalls her father taking all his money, and the stones she laid where it had been kept, under a cloth, to calm her grandfather."
msgstr "Asma waxay xusuusataa aabbaheed oo qaatay lacagtii oo dhan, iyo dhagaxyadii ay dhigtay halkii lacagta lagu hayn jiray, maro hoosteeda, si ay awoowgeed u dejiso."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri notes that he took the very opposite road from the one expected, south of Makkah towards Yemen."
msgstr "Al-Mubaarakfuuri wuxuu xusay inuu qaaday waddadii gebi ahaanba ka soo horjeedday tii la filayay: koonfurta Makkah, dhanka Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq places Asma’s waistband at the cave, and gives it as the reason she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu sheegay in Asma ay suunka dhexda ku kala jeexday godka agtiisa, wuxuuna taas ku sababeeyay in loogu yeedhay Dhat al-Nitaqayn."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘Abbas tells of the web across the cave’s mouth; Ibn Kathir counts this among the best reports of it."
msgstr "Ibn Cabbaas wuxuu ka warramayaa xuub caaro oo daboolay afka godka; Ibn Kathiirna wuxuu qisadan ku tiriyaa wararka ugu wanaagsan ee arrintan laga hayo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the places on the guide’s route, one by one, from below Makkah to the road beyond Qudayd."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu mid mid u magacaabayaa meelihii uu haguhu soo maray, laga bilaabo koonfurta Makkah ilaa waddada ka dambaysa Qudayd."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells of the meeting with al-Zubayr’s caravan of Muslim merchants, and the white clothes he gave the two travellers."
msgstr "Curwa wuxuu ka warramayaa kulankii ay la yeesheen safarkii ganacsatada Muslimiinta ahaa ee al-Zubayr, iyo dharkii caddaa ee uu siiyey labadii socoto."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri tells of the first Friday prayer among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, with a hundred men, in the mosque in the valley."
msgstr "Al-Mubaarakfuuri wuxuu ka warramayaa salaaddii Jimcaha ee ugu horraysay oo lagu tukaday Banu Salim ibn Cowf agtooda, boqol nin oo ku sugnaa masaajidka dooxada."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how each clan was answered, “Let her go, for she is under orders,” until she knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu sheegayaa in qabiil kasta loogu jawaabay, “U daaya, amar baa lagu soo faray,” ilaa ay jilbaha dhigtay iyadoo joogta Banu Maalik ibn al-Najjaar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how he lodged with Abu Ayyub until his mosque and rooms were built, working on them with emigrants and Ansar."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu sheegayaa inuu la degganaa Abuu Ayyuub ilaa laga dhisay masaajidkiisa iyo qolalkiisa, isaga iyo Muhaajiriinta iyo Ansaartuna ay dhismaha ka shaqeeyeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir’s heading for the brotherhood: the Prophet ﷺ paired emigrants with Ansar so each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "Cinwaanka Ibn Kathiir ee walaalaynta: Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu walaaleeyey Muhaajiriinta iyo Ansaarta, si qof kasta oo soo haajiray u helo cid uu ku tiirsanaado."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘A'ishah, a later narrator who does not say who told him, describes women and children singing as the Prophet ﷺ arrived."
msgstr "Ibn Caa’isha, oo ah weriye dambe oo aan sheegin cidda u warrantay, wuxuu tilmaamayaa haween iyo carruur heesaya markii Nebigu ﷺ yimid."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the night he left his house: 27 Safar, in the fourteenth year of his prophethood."
msgstr "Al-Mubaarakfuuri wuxuu taariikheeyaa habeenkii uu gurigiisa ka baxay: 27-ka Safar, sannadkii afar iyo tobnaad ee nebinnimadiisa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri names the three nights in the cave: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Al-Mubaarakfuuri wuxuu magacaabayaa saddexda habeen ee godka: habeenadii ka horreeyey Jimcaha, Sabtida iyo Axadda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the guide’s coming with the two camels to the night of Monday, the first of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "Al-Mubaarakfuuri wuxuu taariikheeyaa imaatinka hagaha oo wata labadii halaad: habeenkii Isniinta, kowdii Rabiicul Awal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah gives the day he came down among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf: a Monday in the month of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "Curwa wuxuu sheegayaa maalintii uu yimid Banu Camr ibn Cowf: Isniin ka mid ah bisha Rabiicul Awal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir sets Ibn Ishaq’s four days, Monday to Thursday, beside ‘Urwah’s report of ten nights and more."
msgstr "Ibn Kathiir wuxuu is barbar dhigaa afarta maalmood ee uu Ibn Isxaaq sheegay, Isniin ilaa Khamiis, iyo warbixinta Curwa ee toban habeen iyo ka badan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates his arrival among Banu al-Najjar to Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal, in the first year of the Hijrah."
msgstr "Al-Mubaarakfuuri wuxuu taariikheeyaa imaatinkiisii Banu al-Najjaar: Jimce, 12-ka Rabiicul Awal, sannadkii koowaad ee Hijrada."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir gives her name, ‘Atikah, and her family, and calls her story well known, through routes that support one another."
msgstr "Ibn Kathiir wuxuu sheegaa magaceeda, Caatiikah, iyo qoyskeeda, wuxuuna qisadeeda ku tilmaamaa mid si fiican loo yaqaan, maadaama silsiladaha werinteedu is xoojinayaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Stones under a cloth"
msgstr "Dhagaxyo maro hoosteeda ku jira"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money, five or six thousand dirhams. When his blind father came, fearing it gone, Asma laid stones in its niche under a cloth and let him feel them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr wuxuu qaatay hantidiisii oo dhan, shan ama lix kun oo dirham. Markii aabbihii indhoolaha ahaa yimid, isagoo ka baqaya in hantidu dhammaatay, Asma waxay dhagaxyo ku ridday godkii ay hantidu ku jirtay, maro ayayna ku dabooshay, dabadeedna way u oggolaatay inuu taabto."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money. To calm her blind grandfather, Asma let him feel stones under a cloth."
msgstr "Abu Bakr wuxuu qaatay hantidiisii oo dhan. Si ay u dejiso awoowgeedii indhoolaha ahaa, Asma waxay u oggolaatay inuu taabto dhagaxyo maro hoosteeda ku jira."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Monday 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"
msgstr "Isniin, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · Sebtembar 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s date. The reports agree on a Monday but differ on the day of the month."
msgstr "Taariikhda Ibn Ishaq. Warbixinnadu waxay isku raacsan yihiin inay Isniin ahayd, balse waxay ku kala duwan yihiin maalinta bisha."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Friday after Quba · Rabi‘ al-Awwal 622"
msgstr "Jimcihii ka dambeeyay Quba · Rabiicul-awwal 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq has him stay at Quba from Monday to Thursday and ride on to Madinah on the Friday."
msgstr "Ibn Isxaaq wuxuu sheegayaa inuu Quba joogay Isniinta ilaa Khamiista, dabadeedna Jimcihii u raacay Madinah."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Verification failed. Try again."
msgstr "Xaqiijintu way fashilantay. Mar kale isku day."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Retry verification"
msgstr "Mar kale isku day xaqiijinta"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s ﷺ bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "Habeenkaas waxay ku sugayeen bannaanka albaabkiisa. ‘Ali wuxuu ku jiifay sariirta Nebiga ﷺ, isagoo ku duuban go’iisa cagaaran."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir, oo ahaa caawiyaha Abu Bakr, ayaa fiid kasta ido u keeni jiray si caano looga liso. Waagu markuu baryo, iduhu waxay mari jireen raadadkii ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some say it was here that Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma split her waistband in two, to tie up their food bag."
msgstr "Qaar waxay sheegaan in halkan ay Asma, gabadhii Abu Bakr, dhexda go’eeda laba u kala jeexday si ay ugu xidho kiishkii cuntadooda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money. To calm her blind grandfather, his daughter Asma let him feel stones under a cloth."
msgstr "Abu Bakr wuxuu qaatay lacagtiisii oo dhan. Si ay u dejiso awoowgeed indhaha la’aa, gabadhiisa Asma waxay u oggolaatay inuu maro hoosteeda ka taabto dhagaxyo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Jimce, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 Sebtembar 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq has him stay at Quba Monday to Thursday and ride on the Friday; a modern biographer worked out the date."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq wuxuu sheegay inuu Quba joogay Isniinta ilaa Khamiista, dabadeedna uu raacay maalintii Jimcaha; taariikh-nololeed-qore casri ah ayaa xisaabiyey taariikhda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari’s report has him come on the morning of the third day; later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Werinta Al-Bukhari waxay sheegaysaa inuu yimid subaxdii maalintii saddexaad; taariikh-nololeed-qorayaashii dambe waxay ku taariikheeyeen habeenkii Isniinta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Monday 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 September 622"
msgstr "Isniin, 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 Sebtembar 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree on a Monday. A modern biographer worked out the date; Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth."
msgstr "Werinnadu waxay isku raacsan yihiin inay ahayd Isniin. Taariikh-nololeed-qore casri ah ayaa xisaabiyey taariikhda; Ibn Ishaq wuxuu sheegay maalintii laba iyo tobnaad."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Kadib nasashadii duhurnimo ee Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d calls it a Tuesday, by his own count of the days; the other reports name no day."
msgstr "Ibn Sa‘d wuxuu ku sheegay inay ahayd Talaado, isaga oo raacaya tirintiisa maalmaha; werinnada kale ma xusaan maalin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as the tribes came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at a place called al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib sat down to listen."
msgstr "Xilli kasta oo xajka ah, markii qabaa’ilku Makkah iman jireen, Nebigu ﷺ wuu u tegi jiray oo wuxuu ugu yeeri jiray Alle. Xilli ka mid ah xilliyadaas, meel la yiraahdo al-‘Aqabah, lix nin oo Yathrib ka yimid ayaa fadhiistay si ay u dhegaystaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, pilgrims came to Makkah. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Sannad kasta, xujaydu waxay iman jireen Makkah. Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu uga warrami jiray Alle, lix nin oo Yathrib ka yimidna way dhegaysteen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At home their Jewish neighbours often warned of a prophet soon to come. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is the prophet they threatened us with.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "Markii ay gurigooda joogeen, deriskooda Yuhuuddu waxay inta badan uga digi jireen nabi dhowaan iman doona. “Alle baan ku dhaarannaye,” ayay lixdii nin isku yidhaahdeen, “kani waa nabigii ay noogu gooddi jireen.” Waxay qaateen Islaamka, dabadeedna dalkoodii ayay ula noqdeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six men said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Deriskooda Yuhuuddu waxay sheegeen in nabi iman doono. “Waa kan!” ayay lixdii nin yidhaahdeen, dabadeedna waxay noqdeen Muslimiin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, those who followed the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ were insulted and harmed by Quraysh, his own tribe, who ruled the town. This is the story of the Hijrah: how they found a new home, and how he made the journey there."
msgstr "Makkah, Quraysh—qabiilkii Nebi Muxammad ﷺ, ee magaalada xukumi jiray—waxay aflagaadeeyeen oo dhibaateeyeen dadkii raacay. Tani waa qisada Hijrada: sida ay guri cusub ku heleen iyo sida uu isaguna halkaas ugu safray."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, the Prophet’s ﷺ own tribe was cruel to the Muslims. This is the story of how they found a new home."
msgstr "Makkah, qabiilkii Nebiga ﷺ ayaa Muslimiinta si naxariis daran ula dhaqmay. Tani waa qisada sida ay guri cusub ku heleen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as tribes from across Arabia came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib, a town to the north, sat down to listen."
msgstr "Xilli kasta oo xajku soo dhowaado, markii qabiillo ka kala yimid dhammaan Jasiiradda Carabta ay Makkah iman jireen, Nebigu ﷺ wuu u tegi jiray oo Allah ayuu ugu yeeri jiray. Xilli ka mid ah, al-‘Aqabah, lix nin oo ka yimid Yathrib, oo ahayd magaalo waqooyi ku taalla, ayaa fadhiistay si ay u dhegaystaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, visitors came to Makkah to worship. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Sannad kasta, dad ayaa Makkah u iman jiray cibaado. Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu uga warrami jiray Allah, lix nin oo Yathrib ka yimidna way dhegaysteen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours used to say a prophet would soon come, and they would follow him against them. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is that prophet.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "Markii ay guryahoodii ku noqdeen, deriskooda Yuhuudda ahi waxay odhan jireen nabi ayaa dhowaan iman doona, iyaguna way raaci doonaan si ay iyaga ula dagaallamaan. “Allah baan ku dhaartaye,” ayay lixdii isu yidhaahdeen, “kani waa nebigaas.” Waxay qaateen Islaamka oo dalkoodii ayay la noqdeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Markii ay guryahoodii ku noqdeen, deriskooda Yuhuudda ahi waxay yidhaahdeen nabi ayaa imanaya. “Kani waa isaga!” ayay lixdii yidhaahdeen, markaasay Muslim noqdeen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came from Yathrib, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night. They pledged to protect him, if he came, as they protected their own families. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "Sannad kasta dad badan ayaa Yathrib ka iman jiray, ilaa ay habeen halkaas kula kulmeen saddex iyo toddobaatan nin iyo laba dumar ah. Waxay ballanqaadeen inay ilaaliyaan haddii uu u yimaaddo, sida ay qoysaskooda u ilaaliyaan. “Anigu idinkaan idinka mid ahay, idinkuna anigaa idinka mid ah,” ayuu yidhi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came from Yathrib at night. They promised to keep him safe, the way they kept their own families safe."
msgstr "Dabadeed, dad badan oo Yathrib ka yimid ayaa habeenkii yimid. Waxay ballanqaadeen inay ilaaliyaan, sida ay qoysaskooda u ilaaliyaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their new home, he told his companions, would be Yathrib, soon to be called Madinah. Group by group these Emigrants slipped away, until few were left but him, his close friend Abu Bakr and his cousin ‘Ali."
msgstr "Wuxuu saaxiibbadiis u sheegay in hoygooda cusub noqon doono Yathrib, oo dhowaan loo bixin doono Madinah. Kooxo-kooxo ayay Muhaajiriintu si qarsoodi ah u baxeen, ilaa ay wax yar oo keliya hadheen: isaga, saaxiibkiis dhow Abu Bakr iyo ina-adeerkii ‘Ali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So the Muslims of Makkah moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to go."
msgstr "Sidaas ayay Muslimiintii Makkah ugu guureen Yathrib, magaalada aynu Madinah u naqaan. Nebigu ﷺ wuxuu sugayay oggolaanshaha Allah si uu u baxo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go too. “Do not hurry,” the Prophet ﷺ told him. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” Abu Bakr hoped it would be the Prophet ﷺ himself, and fed two camels for four months."
msgstr "Abu Bakr marar badan ayuu codsaday inuu isaguna baxo. “Ha degdegin,” ayuu Nebigu ﷺ ku yidhi. “Waxaa laga yaabaa in Allah kuu yeelo wehel.” Abu Bakr wuxuu rajaynayay inuu Nebigu ﷺ laftiisu wehel u noqdo, wuxuuna afar bilood quudinayay laba awr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one noon, at an hour he never came, the Prophet ﷺ came to Abu Bakr’s house. “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “And I am to come with you?” Abu Bakr asked. “Yes.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Maalin duhur ah, saacad aanu caadi ahaan iman jirin, ayuu Nebigu ﷺ guriga Abu Bakr yimid. “Allah wuxuu ii oggolaaday inaan baxo.” “Aniguna ma kula imanayaa?” ayuu Abu Bakr weydiiyey. “Haa.” Abu Bakr farxad ayuu la ooyay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels after three nights to a cave on Mount Thawr, where they would hide. Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, split her waistband to tie up their food, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Waxay kireysteen hage si uu saddex habeen ka dib awrta ugu keeno god ku yaal Buurta Thawr, halkaas oo ay ku dhuuman lahaayeen. Asma, gabadhii Abu Bakr, waxay dhexda maradeeda u kala jeexday si ay cuntadooda ugu xidho, waxaana loogu bixiyey “tii labada dhex-xidh leh”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh feared the Prophet ﷺ would follow his companions. In their council house, their leaders agreed to kill him: a young man from every clan would strike at once, so that no one clan could be made to answer for it."
msgstr "Quraysh waxay ka baqeen in Nebigu ﷺ saaxiibbadiis raaco. Gurigooda shirarka, hoggaamiyayaashoodu waxay isku raaceen inay dilaan: nin dhallinyaro ah oo qabiil kasta ka socda ayaa isku mar weerari lahaa, si aan qabiil keliya loogu ciqaabin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last Allah gave him permission. But the leaders of Makkah, afraid of his message, made a plan to hurt him."
msgstr "Ugu dambayn Allah wuu u oggolaaday inuu baxo. Laakiin hoggaamiyeyaasha Makkah oo farriintiisa ka baqayay ayaa qorsheeyay inay waxyeelleeyaan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. His cousin ‘Ali lay in his bed, so they would think the Prophet ﷺ was inside."
msgstr "Habeenkaas waxay ku sugayeen albaabkiisa bannaankiisa. Ina-adeerkii ‘Ali ayaa sariirtiisa jiifsaday si ay ugu maleeyaan in Nebigu ﷺ gudaha joogo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting the Quran: “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Dabadeed wuu u soo baxay isagoo sacab ciid ah sita, madaxyadoodana ku firdhinaya oo Qur’aanka akhrinaya: “Waxaan daboolnay indhahooda, mana arkaan.” Allah ayaa ka qariyey araggooda, wuuna sii socday."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, throwing a handful of dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Nebigu ﷺ si toos ah ayuu uga dhex baxay, isagoo sacab ciid ah tuuraya, Allahna wuu ka qariyey araggooda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of Abu Bakr’s house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. Madinah lay to the north, but they turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Wuxuu u yimid Abu Bakr, labadooduna waxay ka baxeen albaab yar oo ku yaallay gadaasha guriga Abu Bakr, isaga oo sita dhammaan wixii uu kaydsaday. Madinah waqooyi ayay kaga beegnayd, laakiin koonfur ayay u jeesteen, dhanka Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south first, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Isaga iyo saaxiibkiisii ugu dhowaa, Abu Bakr, ayay gudcurka ku baxsadeen. Marka hore koonfur ayay aadeen, dhanka ka soo horjeeda Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hid in a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Waxay ku dhuunteen god ku yaal Buurta Thawr. Abu Bakr ayaa marka hore galay si uu u hubiyo inuu ammaan yahay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh sent out searchers, and they came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” “What do you think of two,” said the Prophet ﷺ, “when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Quraysh waxay dirtay dad baadha, waxayna aad ugu dhowaadeen oo Abu Bakr hoos ugu yidhi, “Haddii midkood cagihiisa hoos u eego, wuu ina arki lahaa.” “Maxaad ka qabtaa laba qof,” ayuu Nebigu ﷺ yidhi, “marka Allah yahay kan saddexaad?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Men from Makkah searched everywhere, and stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid. The Prophet ﷺ calmed him."
msgstr "Rag Makkah ka yimid ayaa meel kasta baadhay, waxayna istaageen godka dusha sare! Abu Bakr wuu baqay. Nebigu ﷺ ayaa dejiyey."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, who tended Abu Bakr’s sheep, brought the flock to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove it along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Markii habeenku dhacay, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah oo adhiga Abu Bakr raaci jiray ayaa adhigii godka keenay, si labadoodu u helaan caano cusub. Waaberigii wuxuu adhiga mariyey jidkii ‘Abdullah, adhiguna wuxuu tirtiray raadkii cagaha ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep covered up ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir oo Abu Bakr caawin jiray ayaa fiid kasta adhiga keeni jiray si caano looga helo. Waaberigii adhigu wuxuu dabooli jiray raadkii cagaha ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh offered a hundred camels for the two. Suraqah ibn Malik, a horseman of a tribe on the coast road, heard that riders had been seen by the sea. He knew it was them, but kept quiet: he wanted the reward himself."
msgstr "Quraysh waxay labadooda u ballanqaadeen boqol geel ah. Suraqah ibn Malik, oo ahaa fardoole ka tirsanaa qabiil degganaa jidka xeebta, ayaa maqlay in badda agteeda lagu arkay rag fardooley ah. Wuu gartay inay iyagu yihiin, balse wuu iska aamusay: abaalmarinta ayuu isagu doonayay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights they rode on by the sea. A rider called Suraqah raced after them, hoping for a reward."
msgstr "Saddex habeen ka dib, waxay sii raaceen jidka badda agteeda. Nin fardooley ah oo la oran jiray Suraqah ayaa ku daba orday, isagoo rajaynaya abaalmarin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then Suraqah’s horse sank into the ground up to its knees, and he fell."
msgstr "Si xawli ah ayuu u fuulay faraskiisa ilaa uu maqlay Nebiga ﷺ oo akhrinaya. Nebigu ﷺ dib uma eegin; Abu Bakr se marar badan ayuu dib u eegayay. Markaas faraskii Suraqah ayaa dhulka ku dhex dhacay ilaa jilbaha, wuuna dhacay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Shaken, Suraqah begged them for a promise of safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote the promise on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Suraqah oo argagaxsan ayaa ka codsaday inay nabadgelyo u ballanqaadaan, wuxuuna u soo bandhigay sahay. Waxay keliya ku yidhaahdeen, “Meesha aannu joogno qari.” ‘Amir ayaa ballanta maqaar ku qoray, Suraqah-na dib ayuu u noqday, isagoo daba-jooge kasta dib ugu celinaya gurigiisa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him to tell no one where they were, and he sent other searchers the wrong way."
msgstr "Suraqah wuu ka tanaasulay daba-galka. Waxay ka codsadeen inuusan cidna u sheegin halka ay joogaan, wuxuuna baadi-goobayaashii kale u diray jiho qaldan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of a woman called Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Iyagoo gaajaysan oo dalkoodii ka fog, ayay istaageen teendhada haweeney la oran jiray Umm Ma‘bad. Wax cunto ah oo ay siiso ma haysan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked the sheep, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Idaheeda caatada ahi caano ma lahayn. Nebigu ﷺ magaca Allah ayuu ku bilaabay, dabadeedna wuu lisay idihii, qof walbana caano ayuu cabbay!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After they left, her husband came home. She told him of their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Markay tageen ka dib, ninkeedii ayaa guriga yimid. Waxay uga warrantay martidoodii: weji nuuraya iyo hadallo u ekaysiinaya kuul xarig ku taxan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Ansar, the Muslims of Madinah, watched for him until the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Subax kasta, Ansaaru—Muslimiintii Madinah—way sugi jireen ilaa kulaylku dib ugu kaxeeyo guryahooda. Dabadeed nin daar korkeeda joogay ayaa socdaalayaashii oo dhar cad xidhan ku arkay, iyagoo ku dhex biriqaya qiiqa kulaylka: “Waa kan kii aad sugayseen!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, a village just outside Madinah, resting under a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and greeted Abu Bakr, until the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr shaded him with his cloak."
msgstr "Waxay ka heleen Quba, tuulo ku taalla bannaanka Madinah, isagoo Abu Bakr kula nasanaya geed timireed hoostiis. Intooda badan weligood ma arag, markaasay Abu Bakr salaameen, ilaa qorraxdu ku dhacday Nebiga ﷺ, Abu Bakrna go’iisa ku hadheeyay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali caught up with him there. He had stayed three days in Makkah to return what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "‘Ali ayaa halkaas kula kulmay. Saddex maalmood ayuu Makkah ku sugnaa si uu dadka ugu celiyo wixii ay ku aamminteen Nebiga ﷺ. Quba ayuu Nebigu ﷺ ka aasaasay masaajidkiisa, maalin Jimce ahna wuxuu u sii fuulay dhinaca Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah on his camel. Everyone asked him to stay, but he let the camel choose the way."
msgstr "Ugu dambayn, Nebigu ﷺ awrkiisa ayuu ku soo galay Madinah. Qof kastaa wuxuu ka codsaday inuu la dego, balse awrka ayuu jidka u daayay inuu doorto."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried, and there he made his home."
msgstr "Dadku waxay fuuleen meelaha dhaadheer si ay u arkaan. Awrkiisu wuxuu jilba-jabsaday barxad timirta lagu qalajin jiray, halkaasna ayuu degay."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make the Muslims love Madinah as much as Makkah, and even more."
msgstr "Wuxuu Alle ka baryay inuu Muslimiinta ka yeelo kuwo Madinah u jecel sida ay Makkah u jecel yihiin, ama ka sii badan."

